                <pb facs="0091" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v26/pg60"/>

                <head>28. Memorandum From the Principal Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for
                    International Security Affairs (Slocombe) to Secretary of Defense Brown<anchor n="1" xml:id="d28-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-05-24">May 24, 1978</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>
                        ASAT—Suspension of Testing During
                        Negotiations—ACTION MEMORANDUM</item>
                </list>
                <p>As you know, there is substantial sentiment in the building to have the SCC reconsider whether a suspension of testing
                    during the ASAT talks is in the United States’
                    interest. (See Tab A.) The NSC staff refuses,
                    however, to put that issue in the issues paper being drafted for the meeting in
                    the absence of a request to do so by a principal. Simply to ask to have the
                    issue discussed does not prejudge where DOD
                    comes out. Accordingly, I recommend that you call Dave Aaron and ask that suspension of testing be included in the
                    paper as an issue for the SCC.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#bold">
                        Walter Slocombe
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Principal Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">International Security Affairs</hi>
                </p>



                <xi:include href="d28-a1.xml" xpointer="d28-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d28-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d28-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, OSD
                    Files: FRC 330–81–0202, Box 46, 471.96
                    (Apr–June) 1978. Secret. A stamped notation reads: “SEC DEF HAS SEEN.” Under
                        Slocombe’s signature, Brown wrote
                    “5/24. Called Dave A. He will include. HB.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
